      "藥品手冊適應症": "Breast cancer, lymphoma, soft tissue sarcoma, gastric cancer, lung cancer, ovarian cancer.",
      "成人常用劑量說明": "IV. or Intravesical Instillation(Bladder irrigation). \r\r\n1.Standard dose: 75-90mg/m(2) every 21 days.\r\r\n2.Brast cancer: \r\r\n(1).Initial dose range, 100-120 mg/m(2) IV (either given on day 1 or divided equally and given on days 1 and 8), every 3 to 4 weeks; prophylactic antibiotic therapy should be given to patients receiving doses of 120 mg/m(2).\r\r\n(2).CEF-120: cyclophosphamide 75 mg/m(2)/day orally on days 1-14, epirubicin 60 mg/m(2)/day IV on days 1 and 8, and 5-fluorouracil 500 mg/m(2)/day IV on days 1 and 8; repeated every 28 days for 6 cycles; concomitant prophylactic antibiotic therapy should be administered\r\r\n(3).FEC-100: 5-fluorouracil 500 mg/m(2) IV, epirubicin 100 mg/m(2) IV, and cyclophosphamide 500 mg/m(2) IV, each on day 1 and repeated every 21 days for 6 cycles.\r\r\n3.Papillary bladder carcinoma: (1)Intravesical Instillation 50mg for 8 weeks, and reduce dose to 30mg for Epirubicin-induced cystitis. (2)Post-resection prophylaxis: Intravesical Instillation 50mg weekly for 4 weeks, followed by monthly instillations for 11 months. *The Intravesical instillation is administered for 1hours, with the patient repositioning to ensure full bladder coverage.\r\r\n*病人終身建議累積劑量應限制於每平方公尺體表面積投與900 mg Epirubicin。\r\r\n*Dosage adjustment: For p't receiving a divided dose (day 1 and 8): (1) give 75% of day 1 dose on day 8 if ANC 1000-1499, Platelet 75,000-100,000.  (2) Omit the day 8 dose if ANC <1000, Platelet <75,000 or Grade 3/4 nonhematologic toxicity occurs  (3)Hematologic toxicity (platelet nadir count less than 50,000/mm(3), absolute neutrophil count (ANC) less than 250/mm(3), neutropenic fever): Reduce day 1 dose in subsequent cycles to 75% of the day 1 dose given in current cycle. Delay day 1 chemotherapy in subsequent cycles until the platelet counts are ≧100,000/mm(3) and ANC is ≧1500/mm(3).",
