      "成人常用劑量說明": "Individualize dosage. Premedication - IM 0.05-0.1 mg, 30-60 minutes prior to surgery. Adjunct to general anesthesia - IM, IV 0.002-0.05 mg/kg.",
      "兒童常用劑量說明": "Neonatal (Limited data available):\r\r\n-1.Analgesia: \r\r\n(1)Intermittent doses, Slow IV push: Initial 1-2 mcg/kg/dose; may repeat every 2 to 4 hours.\r\r\n(2)Continuous IV infusion: Initial Slow IV push, 1-2 mcg/kg. Usual range: 1-3 mcg/kg/hour.\r\r\n-2.Continuous analgesia/sedation; mechanically ventilated patient: \r\r\n(1)Initial IV bolus 1-2 mcg/kg, then 0.5 to 1 mcg/kg/hour; titrate carefully to effect.\r\r\n-3.Continuous analgesia/sedation during ECMO: \r\r\n(1)Initial IV bolus: 5-10 mcg/kg slow IV push over 10 minutes, then 1-5 mcg/kg/hour; titrate carefully to effect.\r\r\n-4.Endotracheal intubation: slow IV push 1-4 mcg/kg.\r\r\nPediatric\r\r\n-1.Acute pain, Opioid-naive: \r\r\n(1)Infants: IV, initial 1-2 mcg/kg/dose; may repeat at 2-4 hour intervals.\r\r\n(2)Children: IV, initial 1-2 mcg/kg/dose; may repeat at 30-60-minute intervals.\r\r\n(3)Adolescents <18 y/o, <50 kg: Initial IV 0.5-1 mcg/kg/dose may repeat every 1-2 hours.\r\r\n-2.Analgesia for minor procedures/sedation:\r\r\n(1)Infants and Children: IM, IV 1-2 mcg/kg/dose; administer 3 minutes before the procedure; max: 50 mcg/dose; may repeat 1/2 original dose every 3-5 minutes; titrate to effect.\r\r\n(2)Adolescents <18 y/o: IV 0.5-1 mcg/kg/dose; may repeat after 30-60 min; or 25-50 mcg, repeat in 5 minutes if needed.\r\r\n-3.Anesthesia, general; adjunct:\r\r\n(1)Children 2-12 y/o: IM, IV 2-3 mcg/kg/dose.\r\r\n(2)Adolescents <18 y/o: low dose:0.5-2 mcg/kg/dose; medium dose: initial IV 2-20 mcg/kg/dose, Maintenance (bolus or infusion): 1-2 mcg/kg/hour. (For \"fast-tracking\" and early extubation following major surgery, total fentanyl doses are limited to 10 to 15 mcg/kg.) High dose: 20-50 mcg/kg/dose.\r\r\n-4.Anesthesia, general without additional anesthetic agents: Adolescents <18 y/o,IV 50-100 mcg/kg/dose with O2 and skeletal muscle relaxant.\r\r\n-5.Continuous analgesia/sedation:\r\r\n(1)Infants and Children: Initial IV bolus 1-2 mcg/kg followed by continuous IV infusion at initial rate 1 mcg/kg/hour; titrate to effect; usual range: 1-3 mcg/kg/hour.\r\r\n(2)Adolescents <18 y/o, <50 kg: Initial IV bolus 0.5-2 mcg/kg followed by continuous IV infusion at initial rate 0.5-2 mcg/kg/hour.\r\r\n-6.Preoperative sedation, adolescents <18 years: IM, IV 50-100 mcg administered 30-60 minutes prior to surgery or slow IV 25-50 mcg given shortly before induction.\r\r\n*Limited data available in pediatrics <2 y/o.\r\r\n[NICU/SBR]: Analgesia or sedation：Intermittent IV: 0.5-3 mcg/kg/dose q2-4h prn, slow IVP over 5min . Continuous IV dose: 0.5-3 mcg/kg/hr.",
