      "成人常用劑量說明": "slow IV(<50 mg and >10 minutes). Heparin neutralization: Initial, 1 mg of protamine neutralizes ~100 units of heparin; maximum single dose: 50 mg; if aPTT remains elevated, may repeat 0.5 mg of protamine for every 100 units of heparin. \r\r\nCardiac surgery patients: After cardiopulmonary bypass, repeat protamine doses of 25-50 mg may be given to reverse large doses of intraoperative heparin if activated clotting time(ACT) remains elevated or if heparin rebound is a concern; maximum total dose: 3 mg/kg. For heparin rebound, may consider protamine 25 mg/hr continuous IV infusion for 6 hours following the initial dose. \r\r\nEnoxaparin neutralization: Enoxaparin administered in ≦8 hours: Administer 1 mg of protamine to neutralize 1 mg of enoxaparin; maximum single dose: 50 mg. Enoxaparin administered >8 hours to <12 hours ago or if a second dose of protamine is required: Administer 0.5 mg of protamine for every 1 mg of enoxaparin administered; maximum single dose: 50 mg. Enoxaparin administered ≧12 hours: Protamine administration may not be required.",
      "兒童常用劑量說明": "IV(Max. 50 mg/dose). Infants, Children, and Adolescents: \r\r\nHeparin(intravenous) neutralization: \r\r\n[Time Since Last Heparin Dose: Dose of Protamine] \r\r\n<30 mins: 1 mg of protamine per 100 units of heparin; \r\r\n30-60 mins: 0.5-0.75 mg of protamine per 100 units of heparin; \r\r\n60-120 minutes: 0.375-0.5 mg of protamine per 100 units of heparin; \r\r\n>120 minutes: 0.25-0.375 mg of protamine per 100 units of heparin. \r\r\nEnoxaparin (intravenous and subcutaneous) neutralization: Enoxaparin dose administered ≦8 hours: 1 mg protamine sulfate neutralizes 1 mg of enoxaparin; \r\r\nEnoxaparin administered >8 hours prior or if it has been determined that a second dose of protamine is required: 0.5 mg protamine sulfate for every 1 mg enoxaparin.",
