      "藥品手冊適應症": "Anesthesia, Intracranial pressure reduction, Seizures.",
      "成人常用劑量說明": "IV 3-5mg/kg as a 2.5% solution. It produce unconsciousness in 15-30 seconds. Initial 100-500mg, repeated if necessary after 20-30 seconds; max dose: 2g.(仿單)\r\r\n*Other recommendations from uptodate/micromedex:\r\r\n1.Anesthesia, induction: IV: 3-6 mg/kg (maximum total dose: 500 mg) 2.Anesthesia, maintenance: IV: 25-100 mg as needed every 10-12 minutes.\r\r\n3.Intracranial pressure reduction: IV: 1.5-3.5 mg/kg/dose; repeat as needed to control intracranial pressure. (uptodate 2024)\r\r\n4.Refractory status epilepticus, IV: initial 2-7 mg/kg administered at a rate of ≦50 mg/min and follow with continuous infusion of 0.5-5 mg/kg/hour\r\r\n5.Seizure, IV: 75-125 mg single dose; for local anesthetic-induced convulsion, 125 -250 mg IV over 10 min. (micromedex0)\r\r\n*Dose needs to be adjusted according to patient's response and factors such as age, sex, weight, preexisting conditions, premedication, and coadministration with adjuvant drugs. \r\r\n*Geriatrics: dose reduction of 50%-67% (micromedex)",
      "兒童常用劑量說明": "1.Anesthesia, induction and maintenance, IV: \r\r\n(1)Neonates: 3-4 mg/kg for initial induction then 1 mg/kg as needed for maintenance.\r\r\n(2)Infants: IV: 5-8 mg/kg for initial induction then 1 mg/kg as needed for maintenance.\r\r\n(3)Children: IV: 5-6 mg/kg for initial induction then 1 mg/kg as needed for maintenance.\r\r\n2.Intracranial pressure reduction: Infants, Children, and Adolescents: IV: 1-2 mg/kg/dose; repeat as needed. (uptodate)\r\r\n3.Refractory status epilepticus: IV: Initial 2-7 mg/kg at a rate of ≦50 mg/min and follow with continuous infusion of 0.5-5 mg/kg/hour. Mechanical ventilation and cardiovascular monitoring required. (micromedex)",
